Advice on when to use these QDR point charges:
These QDR point charges are strictly intended to be used for constructing atom-centered point charge models used in classical force fields.
They partly re-absorb the atomic quadrupoles and dipoles into the point charges, thereby allowing an electrostatic model truncated at monopole order (i.e., an atom-centered point charge model) to more accurately reproduce the electrostatic potential surrounding the material.
For chemical interpretation of electron transfer and for describing the chemical states of atoms in materials, please use the DDEC6 net atomic charges that are not quadrupole-dipole resorbed.

Citation information:
citation for computer program: T. A. Manz, InteractionModels program, 2025 version, ddec.sourceforge.net
citation for method to compute QDR-DDEC6 charges: A. C. Escobosa and T. A. Manz, How well do various QM-derived net atomic charges reproduce the electrostatic potential surrounding a material across multiple geometric conformations?, submitted to RSC Advances, 2025.
 
